---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DesignTodo from './DesignTodo.astro';
import '../styles/caintra.css';
const { locale='en' }=Astro.props; const es=locale==='es'; const root=es?'/es/':'/';
const slides=[9,8,7,6,5,4,3,2,1];
const formats=[['PRESENTATION','Explain / persuade / support conversation'],['MANUAL','Guide / instruct / reference'],['DOCUMENT','Record / organize / communicate'],['MAILING','Announce / direct attention / generate action']];
const caps=['Information Design','Presentation Design','Editorial Design','Documentation','Instructional Communication','Data Visualization','Template Systems','Digital Communication'];
---
<BaseLayout locale={locale} title="CAINTRA — Making complex information easier to use" description="Professional information design, presentations, documentation and communication systems for CAINTRA.">
<article class="ct">
<header class="ct-hero ct-wrap"><a href={`${root}#projects`}>← {es?'Todos los proyectos':'All projects'}</a><div class="ct-meta"><span>CAINTRA / INDUSTRY · COMMUNICATION · INFORMATION</span><span>NUEVO LEÓN, MEXICO</span></div><h1>Making complex information<br/><em>easier to use.</em></h1><div class="ct-intro"><p>Institutional communication rarely exists in a single format. Presentations need to support meetings and decisions. Manuals need to guide people through processes. Digital campaigns need to communicate quickly. Documents need to remain readable after dozens of pages.</p><p>My work for CAINTRA extended across presentations, documentation, training material and digital communication, translating different types of information into a consistent visual language.</p></div><span class="ct-badge">Original professional communication work</span></header>
<div class="ct-hero-system ct-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí hero Caintra information system"/><div class="hero-slide"><small>CAINTRA / EXECUTIVE COMMUNICATION</small><h2>Industry<br/>in common.</h2><div class="bars"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><span>REPORT / 2022</span></div><div class="hero-doc"><header><b>01</b><span>INFORMATION<br/>SYSTEM</span></header><h3>Clear documents<br/>make work move.</h3><div class="doc-lines"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div></div><img src="/projects/caintra/Slider-Designer-powerPoint-9.webp" alt="Original CAINTRA presentation work"/><div class="hero-mail"><small>MAIL / UPDATE</small><b>WHAT MATTERS<br/>NOW →</b></div></div>

<section class="ct-section ct-wrap"><b>01</b><div><small>01 / CONTEXT</small><h2>Different information.<br/>Different audiences.<br/><em>One institution.</em></h2><p>An industrial organization produces communication for many situations. Some information needs to be understood in seconds; some needs to support a presentation; some needs to remain useful across dozens of pages; some needs to guide a user through a process.</p></div></section>
<div class="ct-format-map ct-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí composición Information → Presentation / Document / Manual / Email"/><header>INFORMATION <span>↓</span></header>{formats.map(([a,b],i)=><article><small>0{i+1}</small><h3>{a}</h3><p>{b}</p></article>)}</div>

<section class="ct-section ct-wrap"><b>02</b><div><small>02 / INFORMATION DESIGN</small><h2>The difficult part is rarely the decoration.</h2><p>Corporate information arrives in imperfect forms: long paragraphs, tables, screenshots, processes, statistics, instructions and technical language. The designer's role is to establish hierarchy before style: what needs to be understood first, what belongs together, and what can become a diagram.</p></div></section>
<div class="ct-raw ct-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: seleccionar aquí ejemplo raw → structured"/><div class="raw-text"><small>RAW INPUT / UNSTRUCTURED</small><p>Multiple activities must be completed according to the conditions described in the document. Users should complete the information and submit it after the corresponding review has taken place...</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Process</td><td>Pending</td><td>Observation</td></tr><tr><td>Registration</td><td>Yes</td><td>Review</td></tr></tbody></table></div><i>→</i><div class="structured"><small>STRUCTURED INFORMATION</small><h3>Complete the process in four steps.</h3>{['Confirm the required information','Select the relevant profile','Review before submission','Submit and retain record'].map((x,i)=><span><b>0{i+1}</b>{x}</span>)}</div></div>

<section class="ct-section ct-wrap"><b>03</b><div><small>03 / PRESENTATION DESIGN</small><span class="ct-badge">Original professional work</span><h2>Presentations are working tools, not decoration for meetings.</h2><p>A presentation must establish pace, allow scanning from a distance and give the presenter structure without competing with the conversation.</p></div></section>
<div class="ct-slides ct-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: colocar aquí selección de PowerPoints originales"/>{slides.slice(0,5).map((n,i)=><figure class:list={{large:i===0}}><img src={`/projects/caintra/Slider-Designer-powerPoint-${n}.webp`} alt="Original CAINTRA presentation slide" loading={i?'lazy':'eager'}/><figcaption>ORIGINAL PRESENTATION / SLIDE 0{n}</figcaption></figure>)}</div>

<section class="ct-section ct-wrap"><b>04</b><div><small>04 / PRESENTATION RHYTHM</small><h2>A presentation needs pace, not one repeated layout.</h2><p>Large statements, evidence, comparison, process and closing slides each carry a different kind of attention. A varied sequence keeps the room oriented and makes information easier to retain.</p></div></section>
<div class="ct-sequence ct-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: crear aquí secuencia de 20 slides"/>{['OPEN','CONTEXT','DATA','COMPARISON','PROCESS','DECISION','CLOSE'].map((x,i)=><article><span>0{i+1}</span><h3>{x}</h3><p>{['Frame the issue','Establish the conditions','Make evidence visible','Clarify difference','Show sequence','Focus attention','Leave direction'][i]}</p></article>)}</div>

<section class="ct-section ct-wrap"><b>05</b><div><small>05 / DATA & DECISIONS</small><h2>Show the relationship, not just the number.</h2><p>Data becomes useful when the visual structure answers a question. Charts, comparisons and tables need a stated purpose: direction, difference, distribution, sequence or priority.</p></div></section>
<div class="ct-data ct-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: colocar aquí slides de datos reales"/><div><small>COMPARISON / EXAMPLE</small><h3>Participation by period</h3><div class="ct-chart">{[52,83,38,71,92,64].map((x,i)=><span style={`height:${x}%`}><b>{x}</b><i>0{i+1}</i></span>)}</div></div><aside><small>DATA TABLE</small><table><thead><tr><th>AREA</th><th>STATUS</th><th>CHANGE</th></tr></thead><tbody>{['Operational','Process','Communication','Training'].map((x,i)=><tr><td>{x}</td><td>{['Active','Review','Active','Planned'][i]}</td><td>+0{i+2}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table><p>Numbers shown here are illustrative layout content, not reported CAINTRA results.</p></aside></div>

<section class="ct-section ct-wrap"><b>06</b><div><small>06 / DOCUMENT DESIGN</small><h2>A document becomes useful when readers can find their way through it.</h2><p>Long documents need navigation, content hierarchy, repeatable page structures and enough restraint for the material to remain readable after the first page.</p></div></section>
<div class="ct-doc-pages ct-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: colocar aquí documentos PDF originales"/><article class="doc-cover"><small>CAINTRA / DOCUMENT 01</small><h2>Information<br/>that moves.</h2><span>Institutional communication / selected work</span></article><article class="doc-index"><small>CONTENTS</small>{['Context and scope','Key information','Process and roles','Reference tables','Appendix'].map((x,i)=><span><b>0{i+1}</b>{x}<i>{12+i*8}</i></span>)}</article><article class="doc-text"><small>03 / PROCESS</small><h3>Read, review, act.</h3><p>Clear hierarchy lets the document carry instruction without requiring every page to start from zero.</p><div><i></i><i></i><i></i></div></article></div>

<section class="ct-section ct-wrap"><b>07</b><div><small>07 / GROW DOCUMENTATION</small><span class="ct-badge">Original professional work</span><h2>Software documentation is part of the product experience.</h2><p>When users encounter a process through documentation, the manual becomes part of the product. It needs to explain the task, not simply archive screenshots.</p></div></section>
<div class="ct-grow ct-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: colocar aquí manual GROW completo"/><header><b>GROW</b><span>USER GUIDE / ORIGINAL DOCUMENTATION WORK</span><strong>PAGE 24</strong></header><main><div><small>MODULE / PROFILE</small><h2>Complete your information.</h2><p>Use the following steps to review and update the corresponding fields.</p><ol>{['Access the module','Select the profile','Complete the information','Review','Submit'].map((x,i)=><li><b>0{i+1}</b>{x}</li>)}</ol></div><aside><div class="grow-screen"><header>GROW / PROFILE</header><p>Personal information</p><i></i><i></i><i></i><button>Save changes</button></div><span>FIG. 04 / PROFILE MODULE</span></aside></main></div>

<section class="ct-section ct-wrap"><b>08</b><div><small>08 / MANUAL STRUCTURE</small><h2>Documentation needs a reliable page system.</h2><p>A strong manual lets a reader recognize where they are, what the page is for and what action follows next.</p></div></section>
<div class="ct-manual ct-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: seleccionar aquí procedimiento GROW paso a paso"/>{[['01','ACCESS THE MODULE'],['02','SELECT THE PROFILE'],['03','COMPLETE INFORMATION'],['04','REVIEW'],['05','SUBMIT']].map(([a,b])=><article><span>{a}</span><h3>{b}</h3><div></div><p>One clear action, supported by image, annotation and exception.</p></article>)}</div>

<section class="ct-section ct-wrap"><b>09</b><div><small>09 / TEMPLATE LANGUAGE</small><span class="ct-badge">Contemporary system extraction</span><h2>Consistency is not repetition.</h2><p>Recurring presentation and document elements can share a visual grammar while allowing each communication to retain the structure its content needs.</p></div></section>
<div class="ct-template ct-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: extraer aquí presentation template system"/><header><span>CAINTRA COMMUNICATION KIT</span><b>CONTEMPORARY SYSTEM EXTRACTION</b></header><div>{[['TITLE','Frame the subject'],['SECTION','Change pace'],['DATA','Make evidence visible'],['PROCESS','Show sequence'],['TABLE','Support reference'],['CLOSE','Leave direction']].map(([a,b])=><article><small>{a}</small><h3>{b}</h3><i></i></article>)}</div></div>

<section class="ct-section ct-wrap"><b>10</b><div><small>10 / INSTRUCTIONAL INFORMATION</small><h2>Turn actions into a visible sequence.</h2><p>Step numbers establish sequence. Screenshots establish location. Annotations establish attention. The visual hierarchy mirrors the order of the task and reduces interpretation.</p></div></section>
<div class="ct-annotated ct-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: mostrar aquí screenshot raw → annotated → manual"/><div><small>RAW SCREENSHOT</small><div class="screen-raw"><i></i><i></i><i></i><b>Form title</b></div></div><i>→</i><div><small>ANNOTATED SCREENSHOT</small><div class="screen-anno"><b>1</b><b>2</b><b>3</b><i></i><i></i><i></i></div></div><i>→</i><div><small>FINAL MANUAL PAGE</small><div class="screen-page"><span>STEP 03</span><h3>Complete the information</h3><p>Confirm each required field before moving forward.</p></div></div></div>

<section class="ct-section ct-wrap"><b>11</b><div><small>11 / ONBOARDING MATERIAL</small><h2>Help new people understand the organization faster.</h2><p>Training and onboarding documents establish terminology, expectations, structure, resources and where to find information later.</p></div></section>
<div class="ct-onboarding ct-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: colocar aquí manual de practicantes"/><article><small>PRACTITIONER GUIDE</small><h2>Welcome.<br/>Here is how<br/>the work connects.</h2><span>ORIENTATION / PROCESS / RESOURCES</span></article><div>{['Orientation','Structure','Schedule','Resources'].map((x,i)=><section><span>0{i+1}</span><h3>{x}</h3><p>Clear, retrievable information for a new participant.</p></section>)}</div></div>

<section class="ct-section ct-wrap"><b>12</b><div><small>12 / MAILING</small><h2>From long-form information to a five-second decision.</h2><p>Email communication creates the opposite design problem from manuals. Hierarchy has to become immediate: what happened, why it matters and what the recipient should do next.</p></div></section>
<div class="ct-mailing ct-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: colocar aquí piezas originales de mailing"/>{[['UPDATE','A new resource is available.'],['EVENT','Registration is now open.'],['REPORT','The latest information, in one place.']].map(([a,b],i)=><article><small>MAIL / 0{i+1}</small><h3>{a}</h3><p>{b}</p><span>OPEN →</span></article>)}</div>

<section class="ct-section ct-wrap"><b>13</b><div><small>13 / COMMUNICATION RANGE</small><h2>The same visual language has to survive different densities.</h2><p>A presentation slide may contain twenty words. A manual page may contain five hundred. An email banner may contain seven. The system succeeds when all remain recognizable without forcing them into the same composition.</p></div></section>
<div class="ct-density ct-wide"><div><small>5 SECONDS</small><h3>ANNOUNCE</h3><p>New resource available.</p></div><div><small>5 MINUTES</small><h3>EXPLAIN</h3><p>Presentation / chart / comparison.</p></div><div><small>30 MINUTES</small><h3>GUIDE</h3><p>Manual / sequence / reference.</p></div></div>

<section class="ct-section ct-wrap"><b>14</b><div><small>14 / VISUAL LANGUAGE</small><h2>Hierarchy before ornament.</h2><p>Charcoal establishes structure. Orange highlights priority and movement. Warm neutral backgrounds reduce visual fatigue in dense documents. Typography and spacing handle different volumes of information.</p></div></section>
<div class="ct-tokens ct-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: extraer aquí document system"/><div class="token-type"><small>TYPE SCALE</small><strong>01</strong><h3>Information<br/>with direction.</h3></div><div class="token-colors"><i>#313737</i><i>#F27945</i><i>#F1EEE6</i></div><div class="token-table"><small>TABLE / STATUS</small>{['Priority information','Supporting context','Reference detail'].map((x,i)=><span><b>0{i+1}</b>{x}<i>{['HIGH','MEDIUM','REFERENCE'][i]}</i></span>)}</div></div>

<section class="ct-section ct-wrap"><b>15</b><div><small>15 / DOCUMENT NAVIGATION</small><span class="ct-badge">Contemporary exploration</span><h2>A PDF can behave like a small information product.</h2><p>Clear contents, section markers, cross references and predictable destinations let documents benefit from interface thinking without becoming an application.</p></div></section>
<div class="ct-pdf ct-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí contemporary communication kit"/><nav><b>CONTENTS</b><span>01 Context</span><span>02 Process</span><span>03 Instructions</span><span>04 Appendix</span></nav><main><header><span>GROW / USER GUIDE</span><b>03 / 42</b></header><h2>Review before submission.</h2><p>Use this page to confirm required elements, then return to the appropriate section when more detail is needed.</p><footer><span>← Previous</span><b>Back to contents</b><span>Next →</span></footer></main></div>

<section class="ct-section ct-wrap"><b>16</b><div><small>16 / READABILITY</small><h2>Professional communication has to survive imperfect conditions.</h2><p>Documents and presentations are viewed on different screens, projectors, printers and devices. Strong contrast, restrained color dependency and clear hierarchy make information more durable.</p></div></section>
<div class="ct-contexts ct-wide">{['PROJECTOR','LAPTOP','PRINT','MOBILE PDF'].map((x,i)=><article><small>0{i+1}</small><h3>{x}</h3><div><b>A</b><i></i><i></i></div><p>Hierarchy remains visible.</p></article>)}</div>

<section class="ct-section ct-wrap"><b>17</b><div><small>17 / COMMUNICATION ECOSYSTEM</small><h2>Many deliverables.<br/><em>One communication language.</em></h2><p>Presentations support live communication. Manuals preserve knowledge. Documents organize institutional information. Mailing creates short-form entry points.</p></div></section>
<div class="ct-tree ct-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí final information ecosystem"/><h2>CAINTRA</h2><div>{[['PRESENTATIONS',['Executive','Informational','Data']],['DOCUMENTATION',['Manuals','GROW','Onboarding']],['DOCUMENTS',['Reports','Guides','Institutional material']],['DIGITAL COMMUNICATION',['Mailing','Announcements','Campaign assets']]].map(([a,b])=><article><h3>{a}</h3>{b.map(x=><span>├ {x}</span>)}</article>)}</div></div>

<section class="ct-original"><div class="ct-wrap original-copy"><div><small>18 / ORIGINAL WORK</small><span class="ct-badge">Original professional archive</span><h2>The work as it was used.</h2></div><p>The presentations, manuals, documentation and digital communication shown here were created as professional work for CAINTRA. Together they represent an extended body of information design across different formats and communication needs.</p></div><div class="ct-archive ct-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: colocar aquí gran archivo profesional Caintra"/>{slides.map(n=><img src={`/projects/caintra/Slider-Designer-powerPoint-${n}.webp`} alt="Original CAINTRA professional communication work" loading="lazy"/>)}</div></section>

<section class="ct-section ct-wrap"><b>19</b><div><small>19 / CONTEMPORARY EXTENSION</small><span class="ct-badge">2026 contemporary system exploration</span><h2>Turning years of communication into a reusable system.</h2><p>Looking retrospectively reveals recurring patterns: titles, data, processes, instructions, warnings, navigation and calls to action. This exploration extracts them into a more explicit communication system.</p></div></section>
<div class="ct-contemporary ct-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí contemporary communication kit"/><small>2026 / CONTEMPORARY SYSTEM EXTRACTION</small><h2>PRESENTATION<br/><em>DOCUMENTATION</em><br/>INSTRUCTION<br/>DIGITAL</h2><div><span>SLIDE SYSTEM</span><span>DOCUMENT SYSTEM</span><span>INSTRUCTION SYSTEM</span><span>DIGITAL COMMUNICATION</span></div></div>
<section class="ct-reflection ct-wrap"><b>20</b><div><small>20 / REFLECTION</small><h2>Information design is infrastructure for communication.</h2><p>Organizations run on documents. Presentations carry decisions. Manuals preserve processes. Instructions help people act. When those materials are clear, consistent and usable, design becomes part of how information moves through an organization.</p><div>{caps.map(x=><span>{x}</span>)}</div><small>Original professional work + contemporary communication-system extraction.</small></div></section>
<div class="ct-final ct-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí final information ecosystem"/><small>ONE ORGANIZATION / MANY FORMATS</small><h2>INFORMATION<br/><em>IN MOTION.</em></h2><div><span>PRESENTATIONS</span><span>DOCUMENTS</span><span>MANUALS</span><span>MAILINGS</span></div></div>
<a class="ct-next ct-wrap" href={`${root}project/mindsherpa/`}><span>NEXT PROJECT</span><strong>Mind Sherpa</strong><b>↗</b></a>
</article></BaseLayout>

